en read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nRead all three files with read_file first, then read/reuse complete mechanisms from all three\nbefore the first edit. Source notes are OPTIONAL; current source blocks can be used directly.\nWhen progress says phase=edit, the initial reading and baseline are satisfied. Apply a scoped edit and verify.\nA note may replace original text only after its mechanisms were exposed. Do not repeat full reads to register them again.\n"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Course progress (new evidence below can satisfy pending items):\n{\"phase\": \"read\", \"next_requirement\": \"read_file: deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", \"remaining_count\": 10, \"requests_left\": 8, \"baseline_done\": 0, \"changed_files\": [], \"verified_current\": 0, \"required_checks\": 1, \"unseen_evidence_count\": 0, \"queued_recall_count\": 0}"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}], "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_1", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "python_interpreter", "arguments": "update_plan(items=[{'title':'verify source delivery','status':'doing'}])\nrun_command(argv=['python','-m','pytest','-q'])\nr0=read_file(path='deepinfer/environ.py')\nr1=read_file(path='deepinfer/logger.py')\nr2=read_file(path='deepinfer/engine/st